From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 087] panvk: honour conditional rendering in the tessellation compute loop

Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: The gpu_prerast tessellation loops dispatch VS/TCS/tessellator and the TES draw without the conditional-render predicate. A skipped predicate still has to run both loops and release the arenas, or the next tess draw deadlocks on the arena and ready/free syncs. Zero the copied draw on the first compute iteration when the predicate fails, and skip the vertex/tiler rasterization. Direct draws preserve an immutable recorded source in device memory so td->in_draw zeroing does not destroy replay submissions; the execution-time flag reset clears pass_mem[1] on every submit. Non-inverted executes when the predicate is non-zero, inverted when it is zero; an inherited secondary uses the normalized subqueue flag; biblioklept
Source/Reference: local, work/mesa 1451e2d99cc, work/mesa-tess-predicate
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (0xb8a31030, PAN_ARCH 11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Mesa base range: 1451e2d99ccb144a35fe958b24eaf121fad4288b
